    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>These obersvatiosn were shared by Christine after testing PBR rater removal  JIRA testing. PBR rater removal was pulled out of July release. These observations must be fixed with <a href="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/browse/EZ-294" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/browse/EZ-294</a> </p>

<p>Issue:</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Named Insured:</b>  The below yellow box items must be manually input on ezdocs now, but none of these feed over to the quote/policy.  It seems the Named Insured pull over from UWD?  But these items pulled from UWD do not show anywhere in ezdocs, other than on the quote/policy:.  The Named Insured ideally should pull from UWD.</li>
</ol>




<p> </p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/1509850" alt="image-20260622-162355.png" width="876" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>

<p> </p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Flood &amp; EQ Aggregate Limits of Insurance.</b>  Currently there is a drop down in this section that allow the UW to select either a TERM or ANNUAL Aggregate to apply for Flood and Earthquake.  This drop down is missing when no BRPT sheet is uploaded.  We need a drop down to select TERM or Annual Agg limits for these coverages:</li>
</ol>


<p> </p>

<p> </p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/1509847" alt="image-20260622-162403.png" width="874" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>



<p> </p>

<p> </p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Coverage Extensions.</b> </li>
</ol>


<p>Currently, if the UW puts $0 for a limit under here for any of the coverage extension types, or does not enter a limit for each coverage extension, the extension shows on the quote but with no limit.  Hence, it looks like coverage is just automatically included.  Each coverage type should require a numeric number be entered under the Limit field.  And, if $0 is entered as the limit, then the quote/policy should show ‘Not Insured’ when $0 is entered for the limit.</p>



<p> </p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/1509846" alt="image-20260622-162410.png" width="827" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>

<p> </p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Schedule of Rates – Builders Risk Property – Coverage Extensions:</b>  If this is selected, the UW can enter in a flat premium, which is great.  However, on the quote/policy, ‘Rating Base’ and ‘Monthly Rate per $100’ show as “Not Insured”.  Rather if the UW selects this coverage and puts in a flat premium, ‘Rating Base’ and ‘Monthly Rate per $100’ should just show as empty – as in nothing should show under them on the quote/policy.</li>
</ol>


<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/1509848" alt="image-20260622-162419.png" width="925" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>



<p> </p>

<p> </p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Delay in Completion Coverage Endst Form – ZC 6538 – Waiting period deductibles</b>.        
	<ol>
		<li>a.) If no value is entered for the number of days waiting, or if 0 is entered, then the quote/policy should show ‘Not Insured’ for these items. </li>
		<li>b.) Also, the Delay Aggregate Limit of Insurance should sum up the limit entered for Business Interruption, Rental Value and Soft Costs; that limit should show as the Agg Limit in ezdocs and on the quote quote/policy for the Delay Aggregate Limit of Insurance</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
</ol>


<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="https://jira-zurichna.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/1509849" alt="image-20260622-162429.png" width="765" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>



<p> </p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
